# Windows Command Line Basics

## Overview
This room covered the basics of using the Windows Command Line Interface (CLI) for system management, networking, file handling, and process management.

---

# GUI vs CLI

## GUI (Graphical User Interface)
- Easy to use
- Mouse-based interactions
- User-friendly for beginner

## CLI (Command Line Interface)
- Faster after practice
- Keyboard-based interaction
- Uses fewer system resources
- Useful for automation and remote administration

## Advantages of CLI
- Lower resource usage
- Faster execution
- Easier automation using scripts
- Convenient remote management using SSH

